implementationPlan.description:
TESTS FIRST (DoD 1 and 2). Load test-driven-development. Create moe-vscode/tests/daemon-bindhost.test.cjs with the session's own editing tool (Write/Edit on a Claude seat, apply_patch on a codex exec seat; never a shell write or a subagent).

Harness: copy fixture() and the server helper from tests/daemon-identity.test.cjs:
- ts.transpileModule of src/services/MoeDaemonClient.ts, run in vm.runInNewContext;
- a vscode stub that records warnings, errors and output-channel lines;
- a child_process.spawn stub that records argv;
- client.resolveBundledDaemonPath = () => 'bundled-daemon.js' and client.waitForDaemonInfo = async () => {}.
Give fixture an options bag { configPort = 0, configHost, autoConnect = true }, so getConfiguration answers 'daemon.port', 'daemon.host' and 'autoConnect' from it. Pass the real process, or { ...process } (the spread keeps kill). Every row registers t.after(() => f.client.disconnect()), so no reconnect timer outlives it. A listen helper for '::1' calls t.skip('no IPv6 loopback') on EADDRNOTAVAIL or EAFNOSUPPORT. Each row writes daemon.json as {port, pid: process.pid, startedAt, projectPath: <project>, bindHost} into a mkdtemp project with .moe/.

Rows (exact-value assertions; each must fail at the base commit):
- B1 no collision: a same-project server on [::1]:P that counts /health and /ws; bindHost '::1'; nothing on 127.0.0.1:P. Assert:
  - connect() rejects;
  - f.spawns deep-equals [];
  - daemon.json is byte-identical;
  - exactly one of warnings+errors contains '::1';
  - f.client.manualDisconnect === true, and after f.client.scheduleReconnect(), f.client.reconnectTimeout === undefined (as tests/protected-daemon-provenance.test.cjs:139);
  - the ::1 server saw 0 /health and 0 /ws.
- B2 port collision: B1 plus a server on 127.0.0.1:P answering /health {projectPath:'/other/project'}. Same assertions, and that server also saw 0 /health and 0 /ws.
- B3 LAN literal: bindHost '192.0.2.10' (TEST-NET), nothing listening anywhere. Same refusal; the message contains '192.0.2.10'; no spawn.
- B4 unsafe host text: bindHost '[x](command:workbench.action.reloadWindow)'. Still refused (no spawn, daemon.json kept), but the message contains neither '](' nor 'command:'.
- B5 helper matrix. offLoopbackBindRefusal(record, workspace, windows) returns null for:
  - bindHost missing, '', 42, '127.0.0.1', '0.0.0.0', '::' or 'wsl';
  - pid 2147483646 (dead), 0, -1, 1.5 or '123';
  - a projectPath naming another folder;
  - a record from the other side of WSL: windows=false with projectPath 'D:\\x\\y' and workspace '/mnt/d/x/y'; windows=true with projectPath '/mnt/d/x/y' and workspace 'D:\\x\\y';
  - record null, [] or 'text'.
  It returns a string containing the host for '::1' and for '192.0.2.10', with pid process.pid and projectPath equal to the workspace or absent.
- B6 today's path is kept, and no refusal message appears, for each of:
  - configPort > 0;
  - configHost '[::1]';
  - a missing daemon.json, where connect spawns `start` exactly once, as today;
  - an unparseable daemon.json;
  - an oversized (over 64 KiB) daemon.json.

Run RED in a whole-repo snapshot of the base with only this file overlaid: the step-3 command without its MoeDaemonClient.ts cp. In the step note, record which B rows fail and why. Every other suite must pass unchanged.
